    "description": "Deal Version was scrapped. What Joyce actually wanted was an edit log — enable field history tracking on Deal.\n\n=== IMPLEMENTATION REQUIREMENTS ===\n\n* Enable field history tracking on Deal. Add the History related list to the layout.\n\n* Kobi, Aug 11: 'we can enable something called field history tracking. They'll track whatever fields that we enable. You'll be able to see a list of the changes. But it doesn't necessarily drive up a version code.' Joyce's requirement: 'as long as we have the edit log for who makes updates and stuff.'\n\n* Per the Aug 17 call with Marc, also enable history tracking on status fields generally: 'let's make sure those fields have history tracking enabled so that they can see the progressions.'\n\n=== OPEN QUESTIONS ===\n\n* Which fields get tracked was never specified, and Salesforce caps it at 20 per object. Starting proposal: Deal Status, Effective Start, Effective End, CPA Amount, Monthly Cap, Payout Model, Priority Tier, Operator, Partner, Vertical, Market Country, Market State. Confirm or trim.\n\n=== NOTES ===\n\n* This is the load-bearing half of removing Deal Version — BUILD-164 deletes the field, this delivers what it stood in for. Don't close BUILD-164 without this.\n\n=== SOURCE ===\n\n* Aug 11 call — Joyce/Kobi 53:20-54:07\n\n* Aug 17 Marc call — history on status fields\n\nDependencies: BUILD-164 (Remove Deal Version)\n\nOwner (proposed): TBD\n\nRemember to update the requirements documentation as part of this change.\n\nCreated 2026-08-17 from the Operator/Partner ticket review, approved by Kobi.",
